{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Systems Thinking.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Systems Thinking.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"systems thinking systems thinking","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Systems Thinking.md","fileName":"Systems Thinking.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Systems Thinking","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 14:36\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Systems Foundations]] [[Emergent Systems]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Systems Foundations","Emergent Systems","Reductionism","Holism","System State","System Behavior","Complex System","Emergence","advancedgamedesign.pdf","agilegamedevelopment2e.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Systems Thinking.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Systems Thinking.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"systems thinking systems thinking","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Systems Thinking.md","fileName":"Systems Thinking.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Systems Thinking","heading":"Systems Thinking","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Systems thinking studies both the parts of a system and the unified behavior created by their interactions. It combines the analytic strengths of [[Reductionism]] with the whole-oriented view of [[Holism]].\n\nThe method moves repeatedly among [[System State|state]], [[System Behavior|behavior]], interaction loops, the resulting whole, and its wider context. This makes it especially useful for designing a [[Complex System]], where feedback and [[Emergence]] make isolated parts an incomplete explanation.\n\nIn an organization, systems thinking shifts improvement from individual utilization to the flow of value, information, and decisions across teams. It reveals how structure and communication can shape both development behavior and the architecture of the product.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Systems Foundations","Emergent Systems","Reductionism","Holism","System State","System Behavior","Complex System","Emergence","advancedgamedesign.pdf","agilegamedevelopment2e.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Systems Thinking.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Systems Thinking.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"systems thinking systems thinking","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Systems Thinking.md","fileName":"Systems Thinking.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Systems Thinking","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[advancedgamedesign.pdf]]\n[[agilegamedevelopment2e.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Systems Foundations","Emergent Systems","Reductionism","Holism","System State","System Behavior","Complex System","Emergence","advancedgamedesign.pdf","agilegamedevelopment2e.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}